    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "Crocs' own auditors once doubted the company would survive.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 2.15,
        "window": 2.8,
        "fill": 0.768
      },
      {
        "scene": "doubt",
        "text": "It had just lost $185.1M in one year, right after the clog craze. So how is this clog still on so many feet?",
        "start": 3.1,
        "seconds": 6.63,
        "window": 7.27,
        "fill": 0.912
      },
      {
        "scene": "sales",
        "text": "At the height of the craze, Crocs sold $847.4M worth of shoes in a year. The next year, that fell to $721.6M.",
        "start": 10.37,
        "seconds": 7.96,
        "window": 8.47,
        "fill": 0.94
      },
      {
        "scene": "copies",
        "text": "Its own filing warned of new rivals selling imitations, and it cut its staff to about 3,700.",
        "start": 18.83,
        "seconds": 4.94,
        "window": 5.57,
        "fill": 0.887
      },
      {
        "scene": "stores",
        "text": "But Crocs never dropped the clog. Today its shops sell it from Toronto to Suzhou to Miami.",
        "start": 24.4,
        "seconds": 4.07,
        "window": 4.73,
        "fill": 0.86
      },
      {
        "scene": "comeback",
        "text": "Last year, the company sold more than $4B worth, and the Crocs brand alone $3.33B.",
        "start": 29.13,
        "seconds": 5.4,
        "window": 6.1,
        "fill": 0.885
      },
      {
        "scene": "loop",
        "text": "Ugly or genius: which one is the clog in your closet? Because not long ago,",
